From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mf: A transform's output types carry its input type's attributes -- media sessions play decoded video through the video processor (9414)

The topology loader puts the video processor between a stream the EVR
cannot take as it is and the renderer, then offers the renderer each of
the processor's output types. Those came bare (subtype and frame size):
the EVR's mixer took every one for a compressed type and refused it, and
the loader failed with MF_E_TOPO_CODEC_NOT_FOUND. No media session could
play WMV, MPEG-1/2, MPEG-4 part 2 or uncompressed AVI video, which the
source hands out decoded as I420 or RGB. As the source reader's pipeline
does, a transform's enumerated output types now get the attributes of its
current input type that they lack (frame rate, stride, aperture, all
samples independent, colour information...).
---
--- a/dlls/mf/topology_loader.c
+++ b/dlls/mf/topology_loader.c
@@ -469,16 +469,36 @@
 static HRESULT topology_branch_foreach_up_types(IMFTopology *topology, MF_CONNECT_METHOD method_mask,
         struct topology_branch *branch)
 {
-    IMFMediaTypeHandler *handler;
-    IMFMediaType *type;
+    IMFMediaTypeHandler *handler, *input_handler;
+    IMFMediaType *type, *input_type = NULL;
+    MF_TOPOLOGY_TYPE node_type;
     DWORD index = 0;
     HRESULT hr;
 
     if (FAILED(hr = topology_node_get_type_handler(branch->up.node, branch->up.stream, TRUE, &handler)))
         return hr;
 
+    /* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 9414): a transform's output types carry the
+     * attributes its input type has (frame rate, stride, aperture, "all samples
+     * independent"...), as the source reader's pipeline gives them: the video
+     * processor's bare output types were all taken for compressed by the video
+     * renderer, and a media session could not play any source handing out
+     * uncompressed video the renderer cannot take as it is (WMV, MPEG-1/2/4 part
+     * 2, uncompressed AVI: MF_E_TOPO_CODEC_NOT_FOUND). */
+    if (SUCCEEDED(IMFTopologyNode_GetNodeType(branch->up.node, &node_type)) && node_type == MF_TOPOLOGY_TRANSFORM_NODE
+            && SUCCEEDED(topology_node_get_type_handler(branch->up.node, 0, FALSE, &input_handler)))
+    {
+        if (FAILED(IMFMediaTypeHandler_GetCurrentMediaType(input_handler, &input_type)))
+            input_type = NULL;
+        IMFMediaTypeHandler_Release(input_handler);
+    }
+
     while (SUCCEEDED(hr = IMFMediaTypeHandler_GetMediaTypeByIndex(handler, index++, &type)))
     {
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_TOPO_BARE_OUTPUT_TYPES
+        if (input_type)
+            update_media_type_from_upstream(type, input_type);
+#endif
         hr = topology_branch_connect_down(topology, method_mask, branch, type);
         if (SUCCEEDED(hr))
             hr = IMFMediaTypeHandler_SetCurrentMediaType(handler, type);
@@ -487,6 +507,8 @@
             break;
     }
 
+    if (input_type)
+        IMFMediaType_Release(input_type);
     IMFMediaTypeHandler_Release(handler);
     return hr;
 }
